From e79f283857a2f618d73863e864551fe910d0bdde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:31:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 35/46] Android: give each GL context its own gl4es instance

gl4es (desktop GL over GLES) keeps its GL state in globals and, with contexts made outside
it (wxQt's QOpenGLWidget), cannot tell them apart.  The 3D viewer opened a second time got a
new EGL context while gl4es still held the first one's programs and bindings, and drew
nothing: a black view until the app restarted.

GL_CONTEXT_MANAGER now loads a separate gl4es instance (android_dlopen_ext with
ANDROID_DLEXT_FORCE_LOAD, from the same file in the APK) for every context after the first,
and points glad at a context's instance when it is locked.  The canvases call the new
GL_CONTEXT_MANAGER::LoadGL() in place of gladLoaderLoadGL(), which would load the shared
instance again.  Other platforms are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
